{title: Nearer, My God, to Thee}
{artist: Sarah Adams & Lowell Mason}
{key: G}
{time: 6/4}
{tempo: 76}

Verse 1
[G]Nearer, my [D]God, to [G]thee, [C]nearer to [D]thee!
[G]E'en though it [D]be a [Em]cross that [C]raiseth [D]me,
[G]still all my [D]song shall [G]be: nearer, my [C]God, to thee —
[G]nearer, my [C]God, to [D]thee, [G]nearer to [D]thee!

Verse 2
Though like the wanderer,
the sun gone down,
Darkness be over me,
my rest a stone.
Yet in my dreams
I'd be nearer,
my God to Thee.
Then evermore to be
Nearer to Thee!

Verse 3
Nearer, my Lord,
to thee, Nearer
to thee! Who
to the cross
didst come, Dying
for me! Strengthen
my willing feet,
Hold me in service sweet

Verse 4
Nearer, O Comforter,
Nearer to thee!
Who with my loving Lord
Dwellest with me!
Grant me thy fellowship!
Help me each day
to keep

Verse 5
But to be nearer still,
Bring me, O God,
Not by the visioned steeps
Angels have trod.
Here where thy cross
I see, Jesus,
I wait for thee,
